{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-hceh-5yum-5ojb-ax5r","published":"2026-11-11T18:53:03Z","modified":"2026-11-24T11:30:42.260230037Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-112949"],"summary":"Vitest is a Vite-native testing framework for JavaScript and TypeScript projects. From 2.1.0-beta.7 until 4.1.12 and…","details":"Vitest is a Vite-native testing framework for JavaScript and TypeScript projects. From 2.1.0-beta.7 until 4.1.12 and 5.0.3, an unauthenticated non-browser WebSocket client that can reach a development server using interceptorPlugin can register a manual mock whose attacker-controlled url createManualModuleSource inserts unescaped into generated module source. When the developer browser loads the affected module, attacker-controlled JavaScript executes on the development-server origin. This issue is fixed in versions 4.1.12 and 5.0.3.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"llama-cpp-0","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/llama-cpp-0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0.7.0-r1"}]}],"versions":["0.7.0-r1","0.7.0-r2","0.7.0-r3","0.7.0-r4","0.7.0-r5","0.7.0-r6","0.7.0-r7","0.8.0-r0","0.8.0-r1","0.9.0-r0","0.9.0-r1","0.9.0-r2","0.9.0-r3","0.9.0-r4"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-hceh-5yum-5ojb-ax5r.json"}},{"package":{"name":"llama-cpp-0","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Debian:13","purl":"pkg:deb/dhi/llama-cpp-0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0.6.0-0"}]}],"versions":["0.6.0-0","0.7.0-0","0.7.0-1","0.7.0-2","0.7.0-3","0.7.0-4","0.7.0-5","0.7.0-6","0.7.0-7","0.8.0-0","0.8.0-1","0.9.0-0","0.9.0-1","0.9.0-2","0.9.0-3","0.9.0-4","0.9.0-5"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-hceh-5yum-5ojb-ax5r.json"}},{"package":{"name":"teleport-18-dev","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Debian:13","purl":"pkg:deb/dhi/te